        "timestamp": 1780968582,
        "contenuto_esteso": "Advertisement Donald Trump World United States & Canada Trump booed by crowd at NBA Finals in New York Madison Square Garden crowd erupts in boos as the US president appears on big screens during the national anthem 3 -MIN READ 3 -MIN Listen Associated Press Published: 9:29am, 9 Jun 2026 Updated: 9:32am, 9 Jun 2026 US President Donald Trump was booed loudly by fans inside Madison Square Garden when he was shown on video screens during the national anthem prior to Game 3 of the NBA Finals on Monday night. Trump was shown for several seconds giving a military salute. The boos ended when the US flag followed him on the screens, and fans cheered when New York Knicks players were shown. Mentions of the San Antonio Spurs also elicited loud boos. Trump was watching from Knicks owner James Dolan’s suite, along with granddaughter Kai, personal adviser Boris Epshteyn and Cabinet secretaries Lee Zeldin, Sean Duffy and Doug Burgum. He is the first sitting president to attend an NBA Finals game. Advertisement Trump’s Marine One helicopter flew from his home in New Jersey and landed near Wall Street before his motorcade made its way up through Manhattan and to the arena roughly an hour before tipoff. He encountered a handful of people making rude gestures, and outside the area, one group held signs saying “Trump must go”. He settled into Dolan’s suite shortly afterwards. Advertisement During the afternoon before Trump’s arrival, the New York Police Department and the US Secret Service set up a large perimeter surrounding Madison Square Garden. Fans lined up to get inside the arena more than four hours before tipoff, in a scene more closely resembling New Year’s Eve in Times Square than the usual lead-up to a basketball game. Advertisement Select Voice Select Speed 00:00 00:00 1.00"
